The `bitixel/paycorp` library is an unofficial PHP SDK for the Paycorp REST API, designed to provide PSR-4 autoloading support for the official Paycorp SDK[1].

### Authentication and Configuration
To use the library, you configure your credentials (including the `authToken` and `hmacSecret`) using the `ClientConfig` class[2]. You do not typically need to manually set `curl_setopt` or custom HTTP headers, as the `GatewayClient` abstracts the underlying HTTP communication[2].

**Example Implementation:**
```php
use bitixel\paycorp\GatewayClient;
use bitixel\paycorp\config\ClientConfig;

$paycorp_credentials = [
    'serviceEndpoint' => 'https://xxxx.paycorp.com.au/rest/service/proxy',
    'authToken'       => 'xxxxxxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx',
    'hmacSecret'      => 'xXxxXxxxxxXXXxXx',
    'ClientId'        => '1234'
];

$clientConfig = new ClientConfig();
$clientConfig->setServiceEndpoint($paycorp_credentials['serviceEndpoint']);
$clientConfig->setAuthToken($paycorp_credentials['authToken']);
$clientConfig->setHmacSecret($paycorp_credentials['hmacSecret']);

$client = new GatewayClient($clientConfig);
